Classifier/session production follow-ups
for sure:
- Make message retry atomic. Use a conditional database update from
  FailedRetryable to Pending and continue only when exactly one row was
  updated; otherwise return 409 Conflict. This prevents concurrent retry
  requests from creating duplicate assistant responses.
- Recover stale Pending user messages after a backend crash. Add a background
  cleanup/recovery job that changes Pending messages older than an agreed
  timeout to FailedRetryable.
not sure yet:
- Export SmartPetCare.Classifier metrics through OpenTelemetry/Prometheus. Add
  dashboards and alerts for 429, 503, timeout, quota_exhausted, circuit_open,
  and retry failures.
- If the backend runs in multiple instances, decide whether the circuit
  breaker must have shared state. Use Redis or another distributed store when
  a global circuit is required; otherwise document per-instance behavior.
- Run a pre-deployment smoke test with PostgreSQL and the real Python
  Classifier: apply the migration, verify 429/503 and Retry-After, retry through
  Scalar, and confirm that the same user messageId is reused.
- Upgrade or replace Microsoft.OpenApi 2.0.0 to resolve NU1903
  (GHSA-v5pm-xwqc-g5wc), then run the full test suite.
